~ start
Oat Milk: [$>> animate("talking")]Hi! I made an appointment for today. My name is Oat Milk.

Player: Great! Welcome to Show Pony Studio.

Oat Milk: [$>> animate("smile")]I’m so excited for this! I’ve been wanting to work on my style for ages. 

Oat Milk: [$>> animate("sad")]Two years at the Clip Clop Cafe and some of the regulars are starting to wonder if I have any other clothes besides my classic outfits.

Player: Alright, well let’s try you out in some new styles and see what we can do.

Player: [studio setup noises] [$>> test()]

Player: Ready?
=> END

~ preppy1
Oat Milk: [$>> animate("smile")]Ooooooh yes! It reminds me of hand-me-downs from my mom haha

Player: Your mom has a good sense of style!

Oat Milk: [$>> animate("talking")]It’s just New England old money, but you gotta hand it to ‘em, the clothes are NICE.
=> END

~ preppy4
Oat Milk: [$>> animate("sad")]My parents weren’t always supportive of me just wanting to be a barista.

Player: You know, I had a guy who was in corporate earlier, and I don’t know that he was any happier.

Oat Milk: [$>> animate("talking")]Of course not! But still, it would be nice to have something to connect with my parents on.

Oat Milk: [$>> animate("sad")]God knows it’s not music—they don’t appreciate the dulcet tones of the heavy metal band Horseshoe.
=> END

~ chic1
Oat Milk: [$>> animate("talking")]Oh, I like it! I feel like it’s kind of like my current classics.

Player: Do you think your regulars will be able to tell the difference?

Oat Milk: [$>> animate("smile")]Well, at least it won’t have coffee stains on it!
=> END

~ chic4
Oat Milk: [$>> animate("talking")]Yeah, this would go well with my coffee-colored beanie.

Player: Does it get hot in the summer?

Oat Milk: So hot! [$>> animate("smile")]But it’s my favorite beanie.
=> END

~ rugged1
Oat Milk: [$>> animate("talking")]Wow, I feel like a cowboy.

Player: Yeah?

Oat Milk: [$>> animate("sad")]Yeah. And by that I mean I feel out of my element.
=> END

~ rugged4
Oat Milk: My mom always said a horse can still be a lady.

Player: Do you feel like you’re a lady?

Oat Milk: [$>> animate("rugged")]I don’t know. She’s not the biggest fan of the barista thing. But she’s trying.

Oat Milk: This might send her over the edge though.
=> END

~ special_item
Oat Milk: [$>> animate("smile")]Oh wow, it’s just like what Black Beauty wears in Horseshoe!!!

Player: Oh, your favorite band?

Oat Milk: Yep!! I feel so cool!!
=> END

~ post_photo_best
Oat Milk: [$>> animate("smile")]Oh my gosh! I really love it!

Oat Milk: [$>> animate("blinking")]To be honest, I’ve been having a lot of trouble finding my style. [$>> animate("sad")]Not just clothes, I mean.

Oat Milk: My parents and I have fought a lot about where I’m going in life.

Oat Milk: [$>> animate("talking")]But I’m really happy doing what I do! I get to help people every day. I’m sure you feel similarly doing this.

Oat Milk: I know it’s not saving lives or changing the world, but we’re making people just a little happier. And that matters, right? Even if other people don’t see it the way we do.

Oat Milk: [$>> animate("smile")]And these clothes make me feel more confident facing the day, while still taking a piece of my parents with me.

Oat Milk: Thank you so much, have a great day!
=> END

